      ],
      "text": "4. Diagnostic approaches for TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI",
      "size": 32.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        144.349609375,
        448.3860168457031,
        185.94960021972656
      ],
      "text": "in children and adolescents",
      "font": "SegoeUI",
      "size": 32.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        219.31861877441406,
        527.4419555664062,
        233.76161193847656
      ],
      "text": "Of the estimated 1.1 million children who developed TB annually, only 399 000 (36.5%) were notified",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        232.5186309814453,
        527.465576171875,
        246.9616241455078
      ],
      "text": "to NTPs in 2020. Under-notification is worst among children below 5 years of age, with only 27.5% of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.999650001525879,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        242.9246368408203,
        527.4346923828125,
        260.1616516113281
      ],
      "text": "(1) children with TB being notified  . These ‘missing’ children are not diagnosed and/or not reported.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        256.12457275390625,
        527.4215698242188,
        273.3616027832031
      ],
      "text": "(1) TB-related mortality among children below 15 years of age was estimated at 226 000 for 2020  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        272.11859130859375,
        527.4100952148438,
        286.5616149902344
      ],
      "text": "Modelling has shown that 80% of TB-related deaths are among children under 5 years of age, and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        282.52459716796875,
        368.6537780761719,
        299.7616271972656
      ],
      "text": "(15) that 96% of children who die of TB, did not access treatment  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        307.0225830078125,
        527.38818359375,
        321.4656066894531
      ],
      "text": "The low case detection rate among (young) children is due to several factors including: the fact that",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        320.2225036621094,
        527.5667114257812,
        334.66552734375
      ],
      "text": "young children have paucibacillary TB and do not excrete enough bacilli to be detectable by available",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.977877616882324,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        333.4225158691406,
        527.4017333984375,
        347.86553955078125
      ],
      "text": "bacteriological tests; the lack of a sensitive point-of-care diagnostic test; difficulties in collecting suitable",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.959927558898926,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        346.62261962890625,
        524.3842163085938,
        361.0656433105469
      ],
      "text": "respiratory samples for bacteriological confirmation; and misdiagnosis due to the overlap of non-",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        359.822509765625,
        527.3916015625,
        374.2655334472656
      ],
      "text": "specific symptoms of TB with other common childhood diseases. Children often first access care at",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        373.0224914550781,
        527.3880004882812,
        387.46551513671875
      ],
      "text": "the PHC level, where there may be little or no awareness and capacity to diagnose and manage",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        386.2225036621094,
        527.4133911132812,
        400.66552734375
      ],
      "text": "children with TB (this includes capacity for sample collection, access to bacteriological tests and CXR,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        399.4225158691406,
        527.4389038085938,
        413.86553955078125
      ],
      "text": "as well as capacity and confidence in making a clinical diagnosis when bacteriological testing is not",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        412.62261962890625,
        527.3991088867188,
        427.0656433105469
      ],
      "text": "available or is negative). In addition, paediatric TB services are often highly centralized at secondary",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        425.822509765625,
        527.468505859375,
        440.2655334472656
      ],
      "text": "or tertiary levels of the health system and managed in a vertical, non-integrated way. TB screening",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        436.228515625,
        451.6864013671875,
        453.46551513671875
      ],
      "text": "(10) is often not systematically incorporated into clinical algorithms for child health  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        460.72650146484375,
        527.3794555664062,
        475.1695251464844
      ],
      "text": "This chapter contains two new recommendations relevant to the diagnosis of TB in children and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        473.926513671875,
        527.4024047851562,
        488.3695373535156
      ],
      "text": "adolescents as well as other valid WHO recommendations that apply to children and adolescents",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        487.1264953613281,
        527.3915405273438,
        501.56951904296875
      ],
      "text": "on TB diagnosis. The two new recommendations relate to the use of the Xpert Ultra assay in gastric",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        500.3265075683594,
        527.4036865234375,
        514.76953125
      ],
      "text": "aspirate and stool specimens for the diagnosis of PTB and detection of rifampicin resistance among",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        513.5264892578125,
        527.4157104492188,
        527.969482421875
      ],
      "text": "children, and the use of integrated treatment decision algorithms  for the diagnosis of PTB in children.  23",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.966699600219727,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        526.7265014648438,
        527.4367065429688,
        541.1694946289062
      ],
      "text": "Prior to 2022, Xpert Ultra had already been recommended for use in nasopharyngeal aspirate (NPA)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        539.926513671875,
        527.48046875,
        554.3695068359375
      ],
      "text": "and sputum specimens; hence, the 2022 recommendation widens the number of specimens that can",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.992998123168945,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        553.12646484375,
        527.2030639648438,
        567.5694580078125
      ],
      "text": "be used and aligns this with the WHO recommendation on Xpert MTB/RIF (which WHO recommends",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.98178482055664,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        566.3265380859375,
        527.4288940429688,
        580.76953125
      ],
      "text": "for use in gastric aspirate, NPA, sputum and stool specimens to diagnose PTB and detect rifampicin",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        576.7324829101562,
        464.4483947753906,
        593.969482421875
      ],
      "text": "(16) resistance)  . The two new recommendations are described in detail in this chapter.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        601.2304077148438,
        119.54681396484375,
        615.6734008789062
      ],
      "text": "Section 4.3",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.956413269042969,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        119.50409698486328,
        601.2304077148438,
        527.2083740234375,
        615.6734008789062
      ],
      "text": "consolidates recommendations from current WHO guidelines on rapid diagnostic tests and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.956413269042969,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        611.6364135742188,
        527.4265747070312,
        628.8734130859375
      ],
      "text": "WHO consolidated guidelines on tuberculosis.  the use of commercial serodiagnostic tests, namely the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
